  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user who keeps « Retours haptiques » on, I want the same taps that vibrated in legacy to vibrate in SwiftHFR.\n\n### Scope\nLegacy plays a light impact in these places, and SwiftHFR plays none. Use `HapticFeedback.live.impact(.light)`, which respects the setting (GAP-149), never `.sensoryFeedback`.\n\n| Where | Legacy @ 87fe0d1c | SwiftHFR today |\n|---|---|---|\n| Favoris « Afficher les sections repliées » / « Tout déplier » | `Favorites.swift:623-629` | `TopicListStateViews.swift:16-17` |\n| Search results arriving | `ForumSearchView.swift:92` | `ForumSearchModel` |\n| Reader « Actualiser », at start and at completion | `MessagesView.swift:5051-5053`, `:5153-5157` | `ReaderPageControls.swift:214-223` |\n\nThe reselect haptic belongs to #426.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Each haptic plays once and is silent with the setting off.\n- [ ] Model-level tests with an injected `HapticFeedback` recorder (as in `HapticFeedbackTests`), failing without the change.\n\nFrom the consistency matrix of #693 (PR #1306, w693).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
